data: {"type": "action", "id": "act3", "icon": "notebook", "title": "Reading documentation", "results": [], "results_units": "Documentation", "started_at": "2026-08-01T09:02:00.442829Z", "ended_at": "2026-08-01T09:02:04.313207Z", "input": {"function_name": ["read_table", "get_google_ads_analytics"]}}

event: final
data: {"type": "action", "id": "act3", "icon": "notebook", "title": "Read documentation", "results": [{"icon": "", "title": "Documentation"}], "results_units": "Documentation", "ended_at": "2026-08-01T09:02:04.590324Z", "output": "async def read_table(table_name: str, dim_name: str = 'all', dim_value: str | None = None, from_day: pandas._libs.tslibs.timestamps.Timestamp | None = None, to_day: pandas._libs.tslibs.timestamps.Timestamp | None = None, limit: int = 200000) -> pandas.core.frame.DataFrame | None:\n    \"\"\"Read a table from the company data lake, filtered by dimension name and value, into a pandas DataFrame.\n\n    This function works for tables with or without dimensions. If there are no dimensions then\n    only `dim_name='all'` is allowed. If there are dimensions this function allows for filtering\n    based on dynamic dimensions. It's particularly useful for social media or analytics data where\n    stats are often categorized by dimensions like country, function, etc.\n\n    Tables with dimensions may have separate records for each dimension value, such as number of\n    impressions per country, or across all audiences (i.e. no dimension filter). All of these different dimensions\n    are available in the same table, in different records. Because of that you need to choose the\n    dimension via dim_name. If you want a specific value of that dimension (e.g. a specific country),\n    you also need to pick the `dim_value`.\n\n    In case you want the data without being aggregated by a specific dimension, you can set `dim_name` to 'all'.\n\n    Filtering by date using the parameters `from_day` and `to_day` narrows down the data and reduces the number of\n    rows to return, otherwise the last two years of data are returned. The limit parameter can be used to further reduce it.\n    For most tables, the data is limited after being ordered by date (desc - most recent). When `dim_name` is \"pages\"\n    the limit is applied to the records with highest page views.\n\n    Args:\n        table_name (str): The name of the table to read from the database.\n        dim_name (str, optional): The name of the dimension to filter by. If 'all', you get the data without being\n            aggregated by any dimension. Defaults to 'all'.\n        dim_value (str, optional): The value of the dimension to filter by. If None, you get the data for all\n            dimension values. Defaults to None.\n        from_day (datetime.date, optional): The start date to filter by. Defaults to 2 years ago.\n        to_day (datetime.date, optional): The end date to filter by. Defaults to current date.\n        limit (int): The maximum number of rows to return. We always return the most recent or, for website page metrics,\n            the records with highest page views. Defaults to 200_000, the maximum limit supported.\n\n    Returns:\n        pd.DataFrame | None: A pandas DataFrame containing the filtered data from the specified table or None if the\n            table does not exist.\n\n    Raises:\n        ValueError: If an invalid dim_name or dim_value is provided.\n\n    Notes:\n        - This function does not deal with temporal dimensions nor with filtering by platform.\n        - If dim_name is not 'all', it checks if it's a valid dimension name for the table.\n        - If dim_value is provided, it checks if it's a valid value for the given dim_name.\n\n    Examples:\n        All Social Posts:\n        >>> df = await read_table('social_posts_with_stats')\n\n        Social Posts created between 2025-08-01 and 2025-08-31:\n        >>> df = await read_table('social_posts_with_stats', from_day=pd.Timestamp('2025-08-01'), to_day=pd.Timestamp('2025-08-31'))\n\n        Daily Social Stats between 2025-01-01 and 2025-06-01 (six months):\n        >>> df = await read_table('social_account_daily_stats', dim_name='all', dim_value=None, from_day=pd.Timestamp('2025-01-01'), to_day=pd.Timestamp('2025-06-01'))\n\n        Daily Social Stats by country (all countries):\n        >>> df = await read_table('social_account_daily_stats', dim_name='country', dim_value=None)\n\n        Daily Social Stats for the US:\n        >>> df = await read_table('social_account_daily_stats', dim_name='country', dim_value='us')\n\n        Daily Website Stats (total):\n        >>> df = await read_table('website_account_daily_stats', dim_name='all', dim_value=None)\n\n        Daily Website Stats up to 100000 rows (limit by latest dates first):\n        >>> df = await read_table('website_account_daily_stats', dim_name='all', dim_value=None, limit=100000)\n\n        Daily Website Page Stats up to 100000 rows (the records with most pageviews):\n        >>> df = await read_table('website_account_daily_stats', dim_name='page', dim_value=None, limit=100000)\n\n    ## Datalake Documentation\n\n    **Updated on:** 2026-08-06.\n    **Pre-filtered Domain:** `example.com`\n\n    ### Overview\n\n    Below you have the documentation for the data tables available in the DOJO AI data lake. This data is collected by DOJO AI, on behalf its customers, from social, content and web analytics platforms.\n\n    We currently support the following platforms:\n\n    - LinkedIn Company Pages / Brands\n    - Twitter\n    - Facebook Pages\n    - Instagram Business\n    - Google Analytics 4\n\n    That data is processed, normalized and aggregated, for each customer, into a set of tables that are easier to query and analyze.\n\n    There are eight types of tables in the datalake:\n\n    - `*_accounts`: Tables with one row per source platform account, with high-level metadata.\n    - `*_account_lifetime_stats`: Table with lifetime stats for each source platform account. It can have multiple rows\n    per platform account, if there are multiple dimensions where the data is aggregated.\n    - `*_account_last_year_stats`: Table with last year stats for each source platform account. It has a single row per platform account,\n    and dimensions, with the latest value for each dimension. This only has metrics that make sense without looking at time windows,\n    such as current followers. This has only one day of data, with the previous year aggregated. Yearly windows may be incomplete\n    (agg_window_in_days < 365) if the platform does not yet have a full year of data. Complement with the `*_account_daily_stats` table.\n    - `*_account_daily_stats`: Table with daily stats for each source platform account. It can have multiple rows\n    per platform account, if there are multiple dimensions where the data is aggregated.\n    - `*_account_event_last_year_stats`: Table with last year event stats for each source platform account. It tracks specific events\n    (e.g., add_to_cart, checkout) and their metrics, aggregated over the last year.\n    - `*_account_event_daily_stats`: Table with daily event stats for each source platform account. It tracks specific events\n    and their metrics on a daily basis, with multiple rows per account for different events and dimensions.\n    - `*_posts_with_stats`: Table with one row per content piece, with stats at the post level.\n    - `*_posts_content_analysis`: Table with one row per content piece, with the text analysis columns,\n    such as sentiment, topics, etc.\n\n    #### Organic vs Paid Influence\n\n    Unless otherwise noted, social metrics reflect total performance and may include both organic and paid influence\n    (e.g., boosted posts or promoted content) when the source platform reports them together. When a breakdown is available,\n    columns are explicitly suffixed with `_organic` and `_paid` (e.g., `facebook_n_page_video_views_organic`, `facebook_n_page_video_views_paid`).\n    In such cases, totals typically include both components.\n\n    #### Platform-Specific Tables\n\n    **Social Platforms (LinkedIn, Twitter, Facebook, Instagram)**\n    - Tables have the `social_` prefix.\n    - Supported tables: `social_accounts`, `social_account_lifetime_stats`, `social_account_last_year_stats`, `social_account_daily_stats`, `social_posts_with_stats`, `social_posts_content_analysis`.\n    - You can use the `platform` column to filter by the platform.\n\n    **Web Analytics (Google Analytics 4)**\n    - Tables have the `website_` prefix.\n    - Supported tables: `accounts`, `account_last_year_stats`, `account_daily_stats`, `account_event_last_year_stats`, `account_event_daily_stats`, with the `website_` prefix: `website_accounts`, `website_account_last_year_stats`, `website_account_daily_stats`, `website_account_event_last_year_stats`, `website_account_event_daily_stats`.\n    - Event stats tables track specific user interactions on your website (e.g., clicks, form submissions, purchases).\n\n    #### Data Availability and Null Values\n\n    Fields in the datalake tables may contain null values. **Null values indicate that the data is not available from the source platform.** This can occur for several reasons:\n    - The metric is only supported for a particular platform and not the others (e.g., `twitter_n_*` fields are specific to the Twitter platform and won't be populated for others)\n    - The platform does not provide that specific metric or dimension, which can happen for:\n        - all records (e.g., the metric is not applicable to certain content types like video)\n        - only some records (e.g., the platform didn't provide this data for those records in particular)\n\n    Null values are a normal part of the dataset and can be handled in queries as needed.\n\n    #### Common Fields\n\n    There are common columns across all tables:\n\n    - `platform`: The platform where the data was collected from. Can be one of the following: facebook, instagram, linkedin, twitter, web.\n    - `id`: The unique ID of the account on the platform.\n    - `domain`: The DOJO AI domain of the account. This uniquely identifies the customer across all tables.\n    - `created_at`: When the underlying entity (e.g. account, post) was created, in UTC.\n    - `updated_at`: When the underlying entity (e.g. account, post) was updated, in UTC.\n    - `recorded_at`: When the table record was calculated and stored in the datalake, in UTC.\n    - `synced_at`: When the table record was last synced with the latest data from the platform, in UTC.\n    This is for accounting purposes only.\n\n    For aggregated metrics tables (usually ending in `_stats`):\n\n    - `dim_name`: The name of the dimension or `all` if it's the overall stats. Examples: `country`, `function`, `interest`.\n    - `dim_value`: The value of the dimension or `all` if it's the overall stats. Examples: `pt`, `Sales`, `Shutterbug`.\n    - `day`: The day of the stats (end-of-day). This is only relevant in data aggregated over time.\n    - `agg_window_in_days`: The number of days the stats are aggregated over, i.e. the window size. For yearly tables, this is typically 365 days but may be less for the most recent window if the platform does not yet have a full year of data.\n\n    For post-level tables:\n\n    - `post_id`: The unique ID of the post on the platform.\n\n    **Important:** All date and timestamp columns are timezone-aware datetime64 in UTC.\n    Use pandas (pd) methods for defining time filters instead of using python datetime directly.\n\n    #### Dimensions\n\n    Segmentation of aggregated data is achieved by using the `dim_name` and `dim_value` columns.\n\n    Whenever a table has these columns, you should always choose `dim_name = \"all\"`, which will give you\n    the records not grouped by any dimension, or you need to pick one of the available dimensions to\n    filter by.\n\n    **IMPORTANT:** If a table has a `dim_name` and `dim_value` column, you **must** choose a `dim_name` and,\n    depending on your use case, choose a `dim_value`. If you don't and you aggregate the data, you will\n    have overlapping records, which will skew the data.\n\n    ### Tables\n\n    In this section we provide documentation for each table in the datalake, using a Pandera model\n    for the schema, using Pandera and Polars types. When manipulating the Pandas DataFrame\n    in the code, you can expect the analogous Pandas types.\n\n    **IMPORTANT:** Tables are not ordered, so you can't assume any order when querying them.\n\n    ```python\n    import polars as pl\n    from pandera.polars import DataFrameModel, Field\n    ```\n\n    #### Table: social_accounts\n\n    **Description:** Information about the source customer's social media accounts in the connected platforms.\n    **Temporal Aggregation:** N/A.\n    **Dimensions:** N/A.\n\n    Each record in the table conforms to the following schema model:\n\n    ```python\n    class SocialAccount(DataFrameModel):\n        \"\"\"A social or content platform account information.\"\"\"\n\n        platform: pl.Enum(categories=[\"linkedin\", \"twitter\", \"facebook\", \"instagram\", \"all\"]) = Field(  # type: ignore\n            description=\"The platform where this account belongs to, or `all` if it's across all platforms\"\n        )\n        id: str = Field(description=\"The unique ID of the account on the platform\")\n        domain: str = Field(description=\"The DOJO AI domain of the account\")\n\n        # Need to convert everything to timezone unaware by converting to UTC and then to naive datetime\n        created_at: datetime.datetime = Field(description=\"The account creation timestamp, in UTC\")\n        updated_at: datetime.datetime = Field(description=\"The account last update timestamp, in UTC\")\n        recorded_at: datetime.datetime = Field(\n            description=\"The timestamp of when this record was calculated and stored in the datalake, in UTC\"\n        )\n        synced_at: datetime.datetime = Field(\n            description=\"The timestamp of the latest synced data used to calculate this record, in UTC\"\n        )\n\n        name: str = Field(description=\"The unique name of the account (e.g. the username or vanity name)\")\n        # we have a specific case where the display name is not available, so it's nullable\n        display_name: str | None = Field(description=\"The full name name of the account (e.g. the display name)\")\n        description: str | None = Field(description=\"The description or tag line of the account\")\n        website: str | None = Field(description=\"The website of the account\", str_contains=\"http\")\n\n        measuring_method: pl.Enum(categories=[\"api\", \"scraping\"]) = Field(  # type: ignore\n            description=\"The method used to measure the account\", default=\"api\"\n        )\n\n        # linkedin specific fields\n        linkedin_staff_count_range: pl.Categorical | None = Field(description=\"The range of the company staff count\")\n        linkedin_organization_type: pl.Categorical | None = Field(description=\"The type of the organization\")\n\n        class Config(BaseConfig):\n            unique = [\"platform\", \"id\", \"domain\"]\n\n    ```\n\n    #### Table: social_account_lifetime_stats\n\n    **Description:** Lifetime stats of the customer's social media accounts, possibly grouped by the different dimensions in the table. Only includes metrics that make sense to measure without a time window (e.g. Total Followers). Use this only for point-in-time values.\n    **Temporal Aggregation:** N/A.\n    **Dimensions:**\n    - all: all\n    - country: 'BE', 'UG', 'MV', 'MK', 'PK', 'DJ', 'SI', 'HK', 'EG', 'IL', and more...\n    - function: 'Information Technology', 'Engineering', 'Real Estate', 'Research', 'Marketing', 'Legal', 'Customer Success and Support', 'Arts and Design', 'Administrative', 'Media and Communication', and more...\n    - industry: 'Investment Banking', 'Medical Equipment Manufacturing', 'Animation and Post-production', 'Aviation and Aerospace Component Manufacturing', 'Insurance Carriers', 'Space Research and Technology', 'Truck Transportation', 'Postal Services', 'Marketing Services', 'Armed Forces', and more...\n    - paid_non_paid: total, unpaid, paid\n    - seniority: 'CXO', 'Entry', 'Owner', 'Training', 'Partner', 'Senior', 'VP', 'Unpaid', 'Manager', 'Director', and more...\n    - staff_count_range: SIZE_501_TO_1000, SIZE_51_TO_200, SIZE_201_TO_500, SIZE_1001_TO_5000, SIZE_11_TO_50, SIZE_2_TO_10, SIZE_10001_OR_MORE, SIZE_5001_TO_10000, SIZE_1\n\n    Each record in the table conforms to the following schema model:\n\n    ```python\n    class SocialAccountLifetimeStats(DataFrameModel):\n        \"\"\"The lifetime stats of a social or content platform account.\n\n        This includes only the stats that are relevant when looking at lifetime totals at a point in time.\n\n        These statistics are aggregated for a specific dimension (e.g. country, language, etc.) or for the overall account ('all').\n        \"\"\"\n\n        platform: pl.Enum(categories=[\"linkedin\", \"twitter\", \"facebook\", \"instagram\", \"all\"]) = Field(  # type: ignore\n            description=\"The platform where this account belongs to, or `all` if it's across all platforms\"\n        )\n        id: str = Field(description=\"The unique ID of the account on the platform\")\n        domain: str = Field(description=\"The DOJO AI domain of the account\")\n\n        dim_name: str = Field(description=\"The name of the dimension or `all` if it's the overall stats\")\n        dim_value: str = Field(description=\"The value of the dimension or `all` if it's the overall stats\")\n\n        recorded_at: datetime.datetime = Field(\n            description=\"The timestamp of when this record was calculated and stored in the datalake, in UTC\"\n        )\n        synced_at: datetime.datetime = Field(\n            description=\"The timestamp of the latest synced data used to calculate this record, in UTC\"\n        )\n\n        # Current follower stats\n        total_followers: int = Field(\n            description=\"The total number of followers at the time of the record\", ge=0, nullable=True\n        )\n        total_following: int = Field(\n            description=\"The total number of accounts the user is following at the time of the record\",\n            ge=0,\n            nullable=True,\n        )\n        total_posts: int = Field(\n            description=\"The total number of posts the user has made at the time of the record\",\n            ge=0,\n            nullable=True,\n        )\n\n        facebook_n_page_follows: int | None = Field(description=\"The number of likes the account's page has\", ge=0)\n        facebook_page_video_view_time_minutes: int | None = Field(\n            description=\"The total time spent watching the account's videos\", ge=0\n        )\n        facebook_n_page_video_views: int | None = Field(\n            description=\"The number of times the account's videos were viewed\",\n            # We're not enforcing ge=0 here because we've seen negative values in the data\n            # ge=0,\n        )\n\n        class Config(BaseConfig):\n            unique = [\"platform\", \"id\", \"domain\", \"dim_name\", \"dim_value\"]\n\n    ```\n\n    #### Table: social_account_last_year_stats\n\n    **Description:** Stats of the customer's social media accounts, possibly grouped by the different dimensions in the table, aggregated yearly, over the last 2 years (at most). It has values for each dimension for each period. Yearly windows may be incomplete (agg_window_in_days < 365) if the platform does not yet have a full year of data. Use this for the yearly values for most metrics.\n    **Temporal Aggregation:** 86 days, 365 days\n    **Dimensions:**\n    - all: all\n    - paid_non_paid: total, unpaid, paid\n\n    Each record in the table conforms to the following schema model:\n\n    ```python\n    class SocialAccountStats(DataFrameModel):\n        \"\"\"The stats of a social or content platform account over a given window of time, measured on a specific date.\n\n        These statistics are aggregated for a specific dimension (e.g. country, language, etc.) or for the overall account ('all').\n\n        Note: Unless explicitly broken out into `_organic`/`_paid` columns, social metrics represent total performance and may\n        include both organic and paid influence (e.g., boosted or promoted content), depending on the source platform.\n        \"\"\"\n\n        platform: pl.Enum(categories=[\"linkedin\", \"twitter\", \"facebook\", \"instagram\", \"all\"]) = Field(  # type: ignore\n            description=\"The platform where these stats are from, or `all` if it's across all platforms\"\n        )\n        id: str = Field(\n            description=\"The unique ID of the account on the platform. In case `platform` is `all`, this should be same as `domain`\"\n        )\n        domain: str = Field(description=\"The DOJO AI domain of the account\")\n\n        dim_name: pl.Enum(categories=[\"all\", \"paid_non_paid\", \"city\", \"locale\", \"country\", \"gender_age\", \"hour_of_day\"]) = (  # type: ignore\n            Field(description=\"The name of the dimension or `all` if it's the overall stats\")\n        )\n        dim_value: str = Field(description=\"The value of the dimension or `all` if it's the overall stats\")\n\n        # Time dimension\n        # we standardize all date and datetimes to the same type so that joins and\n        # df manipulations don't yield errors, when the agents are using them\n        day: datetime.datetime = Field(description=\"The day of the stats\")\n        agg_window_in_days: int = Field(\n            description=\"The number of days the account stats report to\", ge=0\n        )  # TODO: change this to a TimeDelta\n\n        # Time accounting\n        recorded_at: datetime.datetime = Field(\n            description=\"The timestamp of when this record was calculated and stored in the datalake, in UTC\"\n        )\n        synced_at: datetime.datetime = Field(\n            description=\"The timestamp of the latest synced data used to calculate this record, in UTC\"\n        )\n\n        # follower stats\n        total_followers: int = Field(\n            description=\"The total number of followers at the end of the window\", ge=0, nullable=True\n        )\n        total_following: int = Field(\n            description=\"The total number of accounts the user is following at the end of the window\",\n            ge=0,\n            nullable=True,\n        )\n        n_followers_delta: int = Field(\n            description=\"The change in the number of followers since the beginning of the window\",\n            nullable=True,\n        )\n\n        # unique stats\n        n_uniques: int | None = Field(\n            description=\"The number of unique users who viewed the account's content (reach)\", ge=0\n        )\n        n_uniques_daily_avg: float | None = Field(\n            description=\"The average number of unique users who viewed the account's content (reach)\", ge=0\n        )\n\n        # share stats\n        n_impressions: int = Field(description=\"The number of times the account's content was viewed\", ge=0, nullable=True)\n        n_impressions_organic: int = Field(\n            description=\"The number of times the account's content was viewed organically (non-paid)\",\n            ge=0,\n            nullable=True,\n        )\n        n_shares: int = Field(description=\"The number of times the account's content was shared\", ge=0, nullable=True)\n        n_comments: int = Field(description=\"The number of times the account's content was commented\", ge=0, nullable=True)\n        n_likes: int = Field(description=\"The number of times the account's content was liked\", ge=0, nullable=True)\n        n_poll_votes: int = Field(description=\"The number of times the account's content was voted on\", ge=0, nullable=True)\n        n_clicks: int = Field(description=\"The number of times the account's content was clicked\", ge=0, nullable=True)\n        n_clickthroughs: int = Field(\n            description=\"The number of times the account's content was clicked through\", ge=0, nullable=True\n        )\n        clickthrough_rate: float = Field(description=\"The clickthrough rate of the account's content\", ge=0, nullable=True)\n        n_engagements: int = Field(\n            description=\"The number of times the account's content was engaged with\", ge=0, nullable=True\n        )\n        engagement_rate: float = Field(description=\"The engagement rate of the account's content\", ge=0, nullable=True)\n\n        # twitter specific fields\n        twitter_n_url_clickthroughs: int | None = Field(\n            description=\"The number of times the account's content was clicked through\", ge=0\n        )\n        twitter_n_app_clickthroughs: int | None = Field(\n            description=\"The number of times the account's content was clicked through\", ge=0\n        )\n        twitter_n_content_follows: int | None = Field(\n            description=\"The number of times the account's content was followed\", ge=0\n        )\n        twitter_n_content_unfollows: int | None = Field(\n            description=\"The number of times the account's content was unfollowed\", ge=0\n        )\n        twitter_n_card_engagements: int | None = Field(\n            description=\"The number of times the account's content was engaged with\", ge=0\n        )\n        twitter_n_carousel_swipes: int | None = Field(\n            description=\"The number of times the account's content was swiped\", ge=0\n        )\n        twitter_n_qualified_impressions: int | None = Field(\n            description=\"The number of times the account's content was qualified\", ge=0\n        )\n        twitter_n_tweets_sent: int | None = Field(description=\"The number of times the account's content was sent\", ge=0)\n\n        # linkedin specific fields\n        linkedin_n_page_impressions: int | None = Field(\n            description=\"The number of times the account's page was viewed\", ge=0\n        )\n        linkedin_n_page_uniques: int | None = Field(\n            description=\"The number of unique users who viewed the account's page, not the content\",\n            ge=0,\n        )\n        linkedin_n_video_views: int | None = Field(\n            description=\"The number of times the account's video content was viewed\", ge=0\n        )\n        linkedin_n_video_viewers: int | None = Field(\n            description=\"The number of viewers of the account's video content (summed across days, so it may count a viewer more than once)\",\n            ge=0,\n        )\n        linkedin_video_time_watched_minutes: float | None = Field(\n            description=\"The total time spent watching the account's video content, in minutes\", ge=0\n        )\n        linkedin_video_time_watched_for_views_minutes: float | None = Field(\n            description=\"The time spent watching the account's video content that counted towards video views, in minutes\",\n            ge=0,\n        )\n\n        # facebook specific fields\n        facebook_n_page_cta_clicks: int | None = Field(\n            description=\"The number of clicks on the Page's contact info and call-to-action button\", ge=0\n        )\n        facebook_n_page_video_views: int | None = Field(\n            description=\"The number of times the account's video was viewed (at least 3s)\",\n            # NOTE: We're not enforcing ge=0 here because we've seen negative values in the data\n            # ge=0,\n        )\n        facebook_n_page_video_views_paid: int | None = Field(\n            description=\"The number of times the account's video was viewed via ads\",\n            ge=0,\n        )\n        facebook_n_page_video_views_organic: int | None = Field(\n            description=\"The number of times the account's video was viewed via unpaid distribution\",\n            ge=0,\n        )\n        facebook_n_page_video_views_autoplayed: int | None = Field(\n            description=\"The number of times the account's video was viewed via autoplay\",\n            ge=0,\n        )\n        facebook_n_page_video_views_click_to_play: int | None = Field(\n            description=\"The number of times the account's video was viewed via click-to-play\",\n            ge=0,\n        )\n        facebook_n_page_video_repeat_views: int | None = Field(\n            description=\"The number of times the account's video was viewed via repeat views\",\n            ge=0,\n        )\n        facebook_n_page_video_complete_views_30_s: int | None = Field(\n            description=\"The number of times the account's video was viewed (at least 30s or its duration)\",\n            ge=0,\n        )\n        facebook_n_page_video_complete_views_30_s_paid: int | None = Field(\n            description=\"The number of times the account's video was viewed (at least 30s or its duration) via ads\",\n            # NOTE: We're not enforcing ge=0 here because we've seen negative values in the data\n            # ge=0,\n        )\n        facebook_n_page_video_complete_views_30_s_organic: int | None = Field(\n            description=\"The number of times the account's video was viewed (at least 30s or its duration) via unpaid distribution\",\n            ge=0,\n        )\n        facebook_n_page_video_complete_views_30_s_autoplayed: int | None = Field(\n            description=\"The number of times the account's video was viewed (at least 30s or its duration) via autoplay\",\n            ge=0,\n        )\n        facebook_n_page_video_complete_views_30_s_click_to_play: int | None = Field(\n            description=\"The number of times the account's video was viewed (at least 30s or its duration) via click-to-play\",\n            ge=0,\n        )\n        facebook_n_page_video_complete_views_30_s_repeat_views: int | None = Field(\n            description=\"The number of times the account's video was viewed (at least 30s or its duration) via repeat views\",\n            ge=0,\n        )\n        facebook_page_video_view_time_minutes: int | None = Field(\n            description=\"The total time spent watching the account's videos\",\n            ge=0,\n        )\n\n        # instagram specific fields\n        instagram_n_online_followers: int | None = Field(\n            description=\"The number of unique accounts that were online at the specified range.\", ge=0\n        )\n        instagram_n_online_followers_daily_avg: int | None = Field(\n            description=\"The average number of unique accounts that were online at the specified range.\", ge=0\n        )\n        instagram_n_saves: int | None = Field(description=\"The number of times a post was saved\", ge=0)\n        instagram_n_uniques_7_d: int | None = Field(\n            description=\"The number of unique accounts that have seen the account's content in the last 7 days (reach)\",\n            ge=0,\n        )\n        instagram_n_uniques_28_d: int | None = Field(\n            description=\"The number of unique accounts that have seen the account's content in the last 28 days (reach)\",\n            ge=0,\n        )\n\n        class Config(BaseConfig):\n            unique = [\"platform\", \"id\", \"domain\", \"dim_name\", \"dim_value\", \"day\", \"agg_window_in_days\"]\n\n    ```\n\n    #### Table: social_account_daily_stats\n\n    **Description:** Stats of the customer's social media accounts, possibly grouped by the different dimensions in the table, aggregated daily, over the last 2 years (at most). It has values for each dimension for each day. Use this for time-series trends (e.g. daily / weekly / monthly trends).\n    **Temporal Aggregation:** 1 days\n    **Dimensions:**\n    - all: all\n    - paid_non_paid: paid, unpaid, total\n\n    Each record in the table conforms to the following schema model:\n\n    ```python\n    class SocialAccountStats(DataFrameModel):\n        \"\"\"The stats of a social or content platform account over a given window of time, measured on a specific date.\n\n        These statistics are aggregated for a specific dimension (e.g. country, language, etc.) or for the overall account ('all').\n\n        Note: Unless explicitly broken out into `_organic`/`_paid` columns, social metrics represent total performance and may\n        include both organic and paid influence (e.g., boosted or promoted content), depending on the source platform.\n        \"\"\"\n\n        platform: pl.Enum(categories=[\"linkedin\", \"twitter\", \"facebook\", \"instagram\", \"all\"]) = Field(  # type: ignore\n            description=\"The platform where these stats are from, or `all` if it's across all platforms\"\n        )\n        id: str = Field(\n            description=\"The unique ID of the account on the platform. In case `platform` is `all`, this should be same as `domain`\"\n        )\n        domain: str = Field(description=\"The DOJO AI domain of the account\")\n\n        dim_name: pl.Enum(categories=[\"all\", \"paid_non_paid\", \"city\", \"locale\", \"country\", \"gender_age\", \"hour_of_day\"]) = (  # type: ignore\n            Field(description=\"The name of the dimension or `all` if it's the overall stats\")\n        )\n        dim_value: str = Field(description=\"The value of the dimension or `all` if it's the overall stats\")\n\n        # Time dimension\n        # we standardize all date and datetimes to the same type so that joins and\n        # df manipulations don't yield errors, when the agents are using them\n        day: datetime.datetime = Field(description=\"The day of the stats\")\n        agg_window_in_days: int = Field(\n            description=\"The number of days the account stats report to\", ge=0\n        )  # TODO: change this to a TimeDelta\n\n        # Time accounting\n        recorded_at: datetime.datetime = Field(\n            description=\"The timestamp of when this record was calculated and stored in the datalake, in UTC\"\n        )\n        synced_at: datetime.datetime = Field(\n            description=\"The timestamp of the latest synced data used to calculate this record, in UTC\"\n        )\n\n        # follower stats\n        total_followers: int = Field(\n            description=\"The total number of followers at the end of the window\", ge=0, nullable=True\n        )\n        total_following: int = Field(\n            description=\"The total number of accounts the user is following at the end of the window\",\n            ge=0,\n            nullable=True,\n        )\n        n_followers_delta: int = Field(\n            description=\"The change in the number of followers since the beginning of the window\",\n            nullable=True,\n        )\n\n        # unique stats\n        n_uniques: int | None = Field(\n            description=\"The number of unique users who viewed the account's content (reach)\", ge=0\n        )\n        n_uniques_daily_avg: float | None = Field(\n            description=\"The average number of unique users who viewed the account's content (reach)\", ge=0\n        )\n\n        # share stats\n        n_impressions: int = Field(description=\"The number of times the account's content was viewed\", ge=0, nullable=True)\n        n_impressions_organic: int = Field(\n            description=\"The number of times the account's content was viewed organically (non-paid)\",\n            ge=0,\n            nullable=True,\n        )\n        n_shares: int = Field(description=\"The number of times the account's content was shared\", ge=0, nullable=True)\n        n_comments: int = Field(description=\"The number of times the account's content was commented\", ge=0, nullable=True)\n        n_likes: int = Field(description=\"The number of times the account's content was liked\", ge=0, nullable=True)\n        n_poll_votes: int = Field(description=\"The number of times the account's content was voted on\", ge=0, nullable=True)\n        n_clicks: int = Field(description=\"The number of times the account's content was clicked\", ge=0, nullable=True)\n        n_clickthroughs: int = Field(\n            description=\"The number of times the account's content was clicked through\", ge=0, nullable=True\n        )\n        clickthrough_rate: float = Field(description=\"The clickthrough rate of the account's content\", ge=0, nullable=True)\n        n_engagements: int = Field(\n            description=\"The number of times the account's content was engaged with\", ge=0, nullable=True\n        )\n        engagement_rate: float = Field(description=\"The engagement rate of the account's content\", ge=0, nullable=True)\n\n        # twitter specific fields\n        twitter_n_url_clickthroughs: int | None = Field(\n            description=\"The number of times the account's content was clicked through\", ge=0\n        )\n        twitter_n_app_clickthroughs: int | None = Field(\n            description=\"The number of times the account's content was clicked through\", ge=0\n        )\n        twitter_n_content_follows: int | None = Field(\n            description=\"The number of times the account's content was followed\", ge=0\n        )\n        twitter_n_content_unfollows: int | None = Field(\n            description=\"The number of times the account's content was unfollowed\", ge=0\n        )\n        twitter_n_card_engagements: int | None = Field(\n            description=\"The number of times the account's content was engaged with\", ge=0\n        )\n        twitter_n_carousel_swipes: int | None = Field(\n            description=\"The number of times the account's content was swiped\", ge=0\n        )\n        twitter_n_qualified_impressions: int | None = Field(\n            description=\"The number of times the account's content was qualified\", ge=0\n        )\n        twitter_n_tweets_sent: int | None = Field(description=\"The number of times the account's content was sent\", ge=0)\n\n        # linkedin specific fields\n        linkedin_n_page_impressions: int | None = Field(\n            description=\"The number of times the account's page was viewed\", ge=0\n        )\n        linkedin_n_page_uniques: int | None = Field(\n            description=\"The number of unique users who viewed the account's page, not the content\",\n            ge=0,\n        )\n        linkedin_n_video_views: int | None = Field(\n            description=\"The number of times the account's video content was viewed\", ge=0\n        )\n        linkedin_n_video_viewers: int | None = Field(\n            description=\"The number of viewers of the account's video content (summed across days, so it may count a viewer more than once)\",\n            ge=0,\n        )\n        linkedin_video_time_watched_minutes: float | None = Field(\n            description=\"The total time spent watching the account's video content, in minutes\", ge=0\n        )\n        linkedin_video_time_watched_for_views_minutes: float | None = Field(\n            description=\"The time spent watching the account's video content that counted towards video views, in minutes\",\n            ge=0,\n        )\n\n        # facebook specific fields\n        facebook_n_page_cta_clicks: int | None = Field(\n            description=\"The number of clicks on the Page's contact info and call-to-action button\", ge=0\n        )\n        facebook_n_page_video_views: int | None = Field(\n            description=\"The number of times the account's video was viewed (at least 3s)\",\n            # NOTE: We're not enforcing ge=0 here because we've seen negative values in the data\n            # ge=0,\n        )\n        facebook_n_page_video_views_paid: int | None = Field(\n            description=\"The number of times the account's video was viewed via ads\",\n            ge=0,\n        )\n        facebook_n_page_video_views_organic: int | None = Field(\n            description=\"The number of times the account's video was viewed via unpaid distribution\",\n            ge=0,\n        )\n        facebook_n_page_video_views_autoplayed: int | None = Field(\n            description=\"The number of times the account's video was viewed via autoplay\",\n            ge=0,\n        )\n        facebook_n_page_video_views_click_to_play: int | None = Field(\n            description=\"The number of times the account's video was viewed via click-to-play\",\n            ge=0,\n        )\n        facebook_n_page_video_repeat_views: int | None = Field(\n            description=\"The number of times the account's video was viewed via repeat views\",\n            ge=0,\n        )\n        facebook_n_page_video_complete_views_30_s: int | None = Field(\n            description=\"The number of times the account's video was viewed (at least 30s or its duration)\",\n            ge=0,\n        )\n        facebook_n_page_video_complete_views_30_s_paid: int | None = Field(\n            description=\"The number of times the account's video was viewed (at least 30s or its duration) via ads\",\n            # NOTE: We're not enforcing ge=0 here because we've seen negative values in the data\n            # ge=0,\n        )\n        facebook_n_page_video_complete_views_30_s_organic: int | None = Field(\n            description=\"The number of times the account's video was viewed (at least 30s or its duration) via unpaid distribution\",\n            ge=0,\n        )\n        facebook_n_page_video_complete_views_30_s_autoplayed: int | None = Field(\n            description=\"The number of times the account's video was viewed (at least 30s or its duration) via autoplay\",\n            ge=0,\n        )\n        facebook_n_page_video_complete_views_30_s_click_to_play: int | None = Field(\n            description=\"The number of times the account's video was viewed (at least 30s or its duration) via click-to-play\",\n            ge=0,\n        )\n        facebook_n_page_video_complete_views_30_s_repeat_views: int | None = Field(\n            description=\"The number of times the account's video was viewed (at least 30s or its duration) via repeat views\",\n            ge=0,\n        )\n        facebook_page_video_view_time_minutes: int | None = Field(\n            description=\"The total time spent watching the account's videos\",\n            ge=0,\n        )\n\n        # instagram specific fields\n        instagram_n_online_followers: int | None = Field(\n            description=\"The number of unique accounts that were online at the specified range.\", ge=0\n        )\n        instagram_n_online_followers_daily_avg: int | None = Field(\n            description=\"The average number of unique accounts that were online at the specified range.\", ge=0\n        )\n        instagram_n_saves: int | None = Field(description=\"The number of times a post was saved\", ge=0)\n        instagram_n_uniques_7_d: int | None = Field(\n            description=\"The number of unique accounts that have seen the account's content in the last 7 days (reach)\",\n            ge=0,\n        )\n        instagram_n_uniques_28_d: int | None = Field(\n            description=\"The number of unique accounts that have seen the account's content in the last 28 days (reach)\",\n            ge=0,\n        )\n\n        class Config(BaseConfig):\n            unique = [\"platform\", \"id\", \"domain\", \"dim_name\", \"dim_value\", \"day\", \"agg_window_in_days\"]\n\n    ```\n\n    #### Table: social_posts_with_stats\n\n    **Description:** The customer's social media posts with corresponding post-level stats.\n    **Temporal Aggregation:** N/A.\n    **Dimensions:** N/A.\n\n    Each record in the table conforms to the following schema model:\n\n    ```python\n    class SocialPost(DataFrameModel):\n        \"\"\"A post on a social media or content platform.\n\n        It includes the content as well as the lifetime stats of the post at the time of the record.\n\n        Note: Unless explicitly broken out into `_organic`/`_paid` columns, post-level metrics represent total performance and may\n        include both organic and paid influence (e.g., boosted or promoted content), depending on the source platform.\n        \"\"\"\n\n        platform: pl.Enum(categories=[\"linkedin\", \"twitter\", \"facebook\", \"instagram\"]) = Field(  # type: ignore\n            description=\"The platform where this post is from\"\n        )\n        account_id: str = Field(description=\"The ID of the account that made this post\")\n        domain: str = Field(description=\"The DOJO AI domain of the account\")\n\n        post_id: str = Field(description=\"The ID of the post\")\n        post_url: str = Field(\n            description=\"The permalink URL to view the post on its native platform\",\n            nullable=True,\n        )\n\n        created_at: datetime.datetime = Field(description=\"The post creation timestamp, in UTC\")\n        updated_at: datetime.datetime = Field(description=\"The post last update timestamp, in UTC\")\n        recorded_at: datetime.datetime = Field(\n            description=\"The timestamp of when this record was calculated and stored in the datalake, in UTC\"\n        )\n        synced_at: datetime.datetime = Field(\n            description=\"The timestamp of the latest synced data used to calculate this record, in UTC\"\n        )\n\n        text_content: str = Field(description=\"The text content of the post\")\n        language: str = Field(\n            description=\"The language of the post\",\n            str_length={\"min_value\": 2, \"max_value\": 2},\n            nullable=True,\n        )  # ISO 639-1\n        is_paid: bool = Field(description=\"Whether the post is paid or organic (False)\")\n        type: pl.Enum(categories=[\"post\", \"post_url\", \"repost\", \"comment\", \"story\"]) = Field(  # type: ignore\n            description=\"The type of the post\"\n        )\n        content_type: pl.Enum(  # type: ignore\n            categories=[\n                \"text\",\n                \"media\",\n                \"document\",\n                \"article\",\n                \"poll\",\n                \"carousel\",\n                \"multi_image\",\n                \"celebration\",\n                \"short_video\",\n            ]\n        ) = Field(description=\"The type of the content of the post\")\n\n        shared_url: str = Field(\n            description=\"The URI that the post links to (http://, https://, tel:, mailto:, etc.)\",\n            # NOTE: Removed str_contains/str_startswith=\"http\" constraints because posts can legitimately\n            # link to phone numbers (tel:), emails (mailto:), and other non-HTTP URI schemes\n            nullable=True,\n        )\n        shared_url_title: str = Field(description=\"The title of the URL that the post links to\", nullable=True)\n        shared_url_description: str = Field(description=\"The description of the URL that the post links to\", nullable=True)\n        shared_url_thumbnail_id: str = Field(\n            description=\"The ID of the thumbnail of the URL that the post links to\", nullable=True\n        )\n        shared_url_thumbnail_alt_text: str = Field(\n            description=\"The alt text of the thumbnail of the URL that the post links to\",\n            nullable=True,\n        )\n\n        shared_media_title: str = Field(description=\"The title of the media of the post\", nullable=True)\n        shared_media_alt_text: str = Field(description=\"The alt text of the media of the post\", nullable=True)\n        shared_multi_image_alt_text: str = Field(description=\"The alt text of the multi-image of the post\", nullable=True)\n\n        poll_question: str = Field(description=\"The question of the poll of the post\", nullable=True)\n\n        has_all_stats: bool = Field(description=\"Whether the post has all reliable stats\")\n\n        n_uniques: int | None = Field(\n            description=\"The number of unique accounts that have seen this post content (reach)\", ge=0\n        )\n        # for the case of facebook, the source field `post_media_view` isn't available for all posts (null values)\n        # this might be the result of a recent change in the facebook api that introduced this field\n        # (https://developers.facebook.com/docs/pages-api/changelog#november--15-2025)\n        # therefore we make it nullable for now\n        n_impressions: int = Field(description=\"The number of times the post was viewed\", ge=0, nullable=True)\n        n_impressions_organic: int = Field(\n            description=\"The number of times the post was viewed organically (non-paid)\", ge=0, nullable=True\n        )\n        n_shares: int = Field(description=\"The number of times the post was shared\", ge=0, nullable=True)\n        n_comments: int = Field(description=\"The number of times the post was commented\", ge=0, nullable=True)\n        n_likes: int = Field(description=\"The number of times the post was liked\", ge=0)\n        n_poll_votes: int = Field(description=\"The number of times the post was voted on\", ge=0, nullable=True)\n        n_clicks: int = Field(description=\"The number of times the post was clicked\", ge=0, nullable=True)\n        n_clickthroughs: int = Field(description=\"The number of times the post was clicked through\", ge=0, nullable=True)\n        clickthrough_rate: float = Field(description=\"The clickthrough rate of the post\", ge=0, nullable=True)\n        n_engagements: int = Field(description=\"The number of times the post was engaged with\", ge=0)\n        engagement_rate: float = Field(description=\"The engagement rate of the post\", ge=0)\n\n        twitter_n_url_clickthroughs: int | None = Field(\n            description=\"The number of times the post was clicked through\", ge=0\n        )\n        twitter_n_app_clickthroughs: int | None = Field(\n            description=\"The number of times the post was clicked through\", ge=0\n        )\n        twitter_n_content_follows: int | None = Field(description=\"The number of times the post was followed\", ge=0)\n        twitter_n_content_unfollows: int | None = Field(description=\"The number of times the post was unfollowed\", ge=0)\n        twitter_n_card_engagements: int | None = Field(description=\"The number of times the post was engaged with\", ge=0)\n        twitter_n_carousel_swipes: int | None = Field(description=\"The number of times the post was swiped\", ge=0)\n        twitter_n_qualified_impressions: int | None = Field(description=\"The number of times the post was qualified\", ge=0)\n        twitter_n_tweets_sent: int | None = Field(description=\"The number of times the post was sent\", ge=0)\n\n        twitter_in_reply_to_status_id: str | None = Field(description=\"The ID of the post that this post is in reply to\")\n        twitter_in_reply_to_user_id: str | None = Field(description=\"The ID of the user that this post is in reply to\")\n        twitter_in_reply_to_screen_name: str | None = Field(\n            description=\"The screen name of the user that this post is in reply to\"\n        )\n\n        # linkedin specific fields\n        linkedin_landing_page_url: str | None = Field(description=\"The landing page URL of the post\")\n        linkedin_call_to_action_label: str | None = Field(description=\"The call to action label of the post\")\n        linkedin_n_comments_top_level: int | None = Field(description=\"The number of top-level comments on the post\", ge=0)\n        linkedin_n_reactions: int | None = Field(description=\"The number of reactions on the post\", ge=0)\n        linkedin_n_video_views: int | None = Field(\n            description=\"The number of times the post's video content was viewed\", ge=0\n        )\n        linkedin_n_video_viewers: int | None = Field(\n            description=\"The number of viewers of the post's video content (summed across days, so it may count a viewer more than once)\",\n            ge=0,\n        )\n        linkedin_video_time_watched_minutes: float | None = Field(\n            description=\"The total time spent watching the post's video content, in minutes\", ge=0\n        )\n        linkedin_video_time_watched_for_views_minutes: float | None = Field(\n            description=\"The time spent watching the post's video content that counted towards video views, in minutes\",\n            ge=0,\n        )\n\n        # facebook specific fields\n        ## video views and time spent watching\n        facebook_post_video_avg_time_watched_minutes: int | None = Field(\n            description=\"The average time spent watching the post's videos (returns 0 for reshared videos)\",\n            ge=0,\n        )\n        facebook_n_post_video_complete_views_organic: int | None = Field(\n            description=(\n                \"The number of times the post's video was viewed (from the beginning to 97%) via unpaid distribution \"\n                \"(excludes replays and returns 0 for reshared videos)\"\n            ),\n            ge=0,\n        )\n        facebook_n_post_video_complete_views_paid: int | None = Field(\n            description=(\n                \"The number of times the post's video was viewed (from the beginning to 97%) via ads \"\n                \"(excludes replays and returns 0 for reshared videos)\"\n            ),\n            ge=0,\n        )\n        facebook_n_post_video_views: int | None = Field(\n            description=\"The number of times the post's video was viewed (at least 3s or its duration) and includes live views\",\n            ge=0,\n        )\n        facebook_n_post_video_views_organic: int | None = Field(\n            description=\"The number of times the post's video was viewed (at least 3s) via organic reach (excludes replays)\",\n            ge=0,\n        )\n        facebook_n_post_video_views_paid: int | None = Field(\n            description=\"The number of times the promoted post's video was viewed (at least 3s, excludes replays)\",\n            ge=0,\n        )\n        facebook_n_post_video_views_autoplayed: int | None = Field(\n            description=\"The number of times the post's automatically played video was viewed (at least 3s)\",\n            ge=0,\n        )\n        facebook_n_post_video_views_clicked_to_play: int | None = Field(\n            description=\"The number of times the post's video was viewed (at least 3s) after people clicked play\",\n            ge=0,\n        )\n        facebook_n_post_video_views_15_s: int | None = Field(\n            description=\"The number of times the post's video was viewed (at least 15s or its duration, excludes replays)\",\n            ge=0,\n        )\n        facebook_n_post_video_views_60_s_excludes_shorter: int | None = Field(\n            description=\"The number of times the post's video was viewed (at least 60s) for >60s videos (excludes shorter videos and replays)\",\n            ge=0,\n        )\n        facebook_n_post_video_views_sound_on: int | None = Field(\n            description=\"The number of times the post's video was viewed (at least 3s or its duration) with sound on (excludes replays)\",\n            ge=0,\n        )\n        facebook_post_video_view_time_minutes: int | None = Field(\n            description=\"The total time spent watching the post's videos (returns 0 for replays)\",\n            ge=0,\n        )\n        facebook_post_video_view_time_organic_minutes: int | None = Field(\n            description=\"The total time spent watching the post's videos (returns 0 for replays) via unpaid distribution\",\n            ge=0,\n        )\n        facebook_n_post_video_complete_views_30_s_autoplayed: int | None = Field(\n            description=(\n                \"The number of times the post's video was viewed (at least 30s) via autoplay \"\n                \"(excludes replays, returns 0 for reshared videos)\"\n            ),\n            ge=0,\n        )\n        facebook_n_post_video_complete_views_30_s_clicked_to_play: int | None = Field(\n            description=(\n                \"The number of times the post's video was viewed (at least 30s) after people clicked play \"\n                \"(excludes replays, returns 0 for reshared videos)\"\n            ),\n            ge=0,\n        )\n        facebook_n_post_video_complete_views_30_s_organic: int | None = Field(\n            description=(\n                \"The number of times the post's video was viewed (at least 30s) via organic reach \"\n                \"(excludes replays, returns 0 for reshared videos)\"\n            ),\n            ge=0,\n        )\n        facebook_n_post_video_complete_views_30_s_paid: int | None = Field(\n            description=(\n                \"The number of times the post's video was viewed (at least 30s) via ads \"\n                \"(excludes replays, returns 0 for reshared videos)\"\n            ),\n            ge=0,\n        )\n        facebook_n_post_video_ad_break_ad_impressions: int | None = Field(\n            description=\"The number of times an ad was shown during ad breaks in the post's video\",\n            ge=0,\n        )\n        facebook_n_post_video_ad_break_earnings: int | None = Field(\n            description=\"An estimated amount of money earned from ads shown during ad breaks in the post's video\",\n            ge=0,\n        )\n        facebook_n_post_video_ad_break_ad_cpm: int | None = Field(\n            description=(\n                \"The average amount paid by advertisers for 1000 impressions of their ads in the post's video \"\n                \"(also includes amount paid to Facebook)\"\n            ),\n            ge=0,\n        )\n\n        # instagram specific fields\n        instagram_n_saves: int | None = Field(description=\"The number of times the post was saved\", ge=0)\n\n        class Config(BaseConfig):\n            unique = [\"platform\", \"account_id\", \"domain\", \"post_id\"]\n\n    ```\n\n    #### Table: website_accounts\n\n    **Description:** Information about the source customer's website property in Google Analytics.\n    **Temporal Aggregation:** N/A.\n    **Dimensions:** N/A.\n\n    Each record in the table conforms to the following schema model:\n\n    ```python\n    class WebsiteAccount(DataFrameModel):\n        \"\"\"A web analytics account information.\"\"\"\n\n        platform: pl.Enum(categories=[\"web\"]) = Field(  # type: ignore\n            description=(\n                \"The data-source connector this account comes from (always `web` for GA4-measured accounts) — \"\n                \"not GA4's device/app platform (web/iOS/Android)\"\n            ),\n            default=\"web\",\n        )\n        id: str = Field(description=\"The unique ID of the account on the platform\")\n        domain: str = Field(description=\"The DOJO AI domain of the account\")\n\n        created_at: datetime.datetime = Field(description=\"The account creation timestamp, in UTC\")\n        updated_at: datetime.datetime = Field(description=\"The account last update timestamp, in UTC\")\n        recorded_at: datetime.datetime = Field(\n            description=\"The timestamp of when this record was calculated and stored in the datalake, in UTC\"\n        )\n        synced_at: datetime.datetime = Field(\n            description=\"The timestamp of the latest synced data used to calculate this record, in UTC\"\n        )\n\n        display_name: str = Field(description=\"The full name name of the account (e.g. the display name)\")\n        # website: str = Field(description=\"The website of the account\", str_contains=\"http\")\n        industry: str = Field(description=\"The industry of the account\", nullable=True)\n        country: str = Field(description=\"The country of the account\", str_length={\"min_value\": 2, \"max_value\": 2})\n\n        measuring_method: pl.Enum(categories=[\"ga4\", \"semrush\"]) = Field(  # type: ignore\n            description=\"The method used to measure the account\", default=\"ga4\"\n        )\n\n        class Config(BaseConfig):\n            unique = [\"platform\", \"id\", \"domain\"]\n\n    ```\n\n    #### Table: website_account_last_year_stats\n\n    **Description:** Stats of the customer's website traffic, possibly grouped by dimensions such as page or country, aggregated over the last 2 years (2*365 days).\n    **Temporal Aggregation:** 365 days\n    **Dimensions:**\n    - age: 45-54, 25-34, 18-24, unknown, 35-44\n    - all: all\n    - country: 'Netherlands', 'Sweden', 'Finland', 'Poland', 'United Kingdom', 'Romania', 'Switzerland', 'Denmark', 'Australia', 'France', and more...\n    - default_channel_group: Paid Search, Direct, Referral, Organic Social, Organic Search\n    - gender: male, female, unknown\n    - interest: 'Travel/Travel Buffs', 'Lifestyles & Hobbies/Business Professionals', 'News & Politics/Avid News Readers/Avid Business News Readers', 'News & Politics/Avid News Readers', 'Media & Entertainment/Music Lovers', 'Lifestyles & Hobbies/Shutterbugs', 'Banking & Finance/Avid Investors', 'News & Politics/Avid News Readers/Entertainment News Enthusiasts', 'Technology/Technophiles', 'Sports & Fitness/Sports Fans/Soccer Fans', and more...\n    - medium: (none), cpc, referral, organic\n    - page: '/pricing', '/blog', '/book-demo', '/careers/founding-ai-engineer', '/ai-marketing-agent-system', '/blog/guest-refurbed-dojoai', '/careers/founding-engineer', '/company', '/careers/founding-full-stack-engineer', '/', and more...\n    - source: laikaventures.co, google, (direct), linkedin.com, syndicatedsearch.goog, t.co, wake-up-network.com, bing, statics.teams.cdn.office.net\n\n    Each record in the table conforms to the following schema model:\n\n    ```python\n    class WebsiteStats(DataFrameModel):\n        \"\"\"The stats of a website over a given window of time, measured on a specific date.\n\n        These statistics are aggregated for a specific dimension (e.g. country, language, etc.) or for the overall account ('all').\n        \"\"\"\n\n        platform: pl.Enum(categories=[\"web\"]) = Field(  # type: ignore\n            description=(\n                \"The data-source connector these stats are from (always `web` for GA4), or `all` if it's the \"\n                \"overall stats. GA4's device/app platform (web/iOS/Android) is a separate breakdown queried as \"\n                \"`dim_name='ga4_platform'` — the `ga4_` prefix exists to avoid colliding with this column\"\n            )\n        )\n        id: str = Field(\n            description=\"The unique ID of the account on the platform. In case `platform` is `all`, this should be same as `domain`\"\n        )\n        domain: str = Field(description=\"The DOJO AI domain of the account\")\n\n        # Read-path discoverability superset: every dimension queryable live from GA4, not a\n        # producer contract (the dormant ELT pipeline emits a narrower set).\n        dim_name: pl.Enum(\n            categories=[\n                \"page\",\n                \"age\",\n                \"gender\",\n                \"interest\",\n                \"country\",\n                \"source\",\n                \"medium\",\n                \"new_vs_returning\",\n                \"default_channel_group\",\n                \"ga4_platform\",\n                \"operating_system\",\n                \"stream_id\",\n                \"mobile_device_branding\",\n                \"all\",\n            ]\n        ) = Field(  # type: ignore\n            description=\"The name of the dimension or `all` if it's the overall stats\"\n        )\n        dim_value: str = Field(description=\"The value of the dimension or `all` if it's the overall stats\")\n\n        # we standardize all date and datetimes to the same type so that joins and\n        # df manipulations don't yield errors, when the agents are using them\n        day: datetime.datetime = Field(description=\"The day of the stats\")\n        agg_window_in_days: int = Field(\n            description=\"The number of days the stats report to\", ge=0\n        )  # TODO: change this to a TimeDelta\n\n        recorded_at: datetime.datetime = Field(\n            description=\"The timestamp of when this record was calculated and stored in the datalake, in UTC\"\n        )\n        synced_at: datetime.datetime = Field(\n            description=\"The timestamp of the latest synced data used to calculate this record, in UTC\"\n        )\n\n        n_pageviews: int = Field(description=\"The number of page views\", ge=0)\n        n_sessions: int = Field(\n            description=\"The number of sessions initiated by users. A session begins when a user opens the website or app and ends after 30 minutes of inactivity\",\n            ge=0,\n        )\n        n_uniques: int = Field(description=\"The number of unique users who have had at least one session\", ge=0)\n        n_new_users: int = Field(\n            description=\"The number of users (uniques) visiting the website for the first time ever\",\n            ge=0,\n        )\n\n        n_engaged_sessions: int = Field(description=\"The number of sessions where the user was actively engaged\", ge=0)\n        engagement_rate: float = Field(\n            description=\"The number of engaged sessions per number of sessions\",\n            ge=0,\n            nullable=True,\n        )\n        average_session_duration: float = Field(description=\"The average duration of a session\", ge=0, nullable=True)\n        total_engagement_duration: float | None = Field(\n            description=\"The total amount of time (in seconds) your website or app was in the foreground of users` devices.\",\n            ge=0,\n        )\n        total_revenue: float = Field(\n            description=\"The revenue generated by users, including purchases and other monetary transactions on the website. Can be negative due to product returns\",\n        )\n\n        class Config(BaseConfig):\n            unique = [\"platform\", \"id\", \"domain\", \"dim_name\", \"dim_value\", \"day\"]\n\n    ```\n\n    #### Table: website_account_daily_stats\n\n    **Description:** Stats of the customer's website traffic, possibly grouped by dimensions such as page or country, aggregated over the last 2 years (2*365 days).\n    **Temporal Aggregation:** 1 days\n    **Dimensions:**\n    - age: unknown, 25-34, 18-24, 45-54, 35-44, 55-64\n    - all: all\n    - country: Portugal, United States, United Kingdom, Germany, India, Australia, Canada, (not set), Congo - Kinshasa\n    - default_channel_group: Direct, Organic Search, Organic Social, Referral, Paid Search\n    - gender: male, female, unknown\n    - interest: 'Technology/Technophiles', 'Banking & Finance/Avid Investors', 'Lifestyles & Hobbies/Business Professionals', 'News & Politics/Avid News Readers/Avid Business News Readers', 'Sports & Fitness/Sports Fans/Soccer Fans', 'News & Politics/Avid News Readers', 'Travel/Travel Buffs', 'Lifestyles & Hobbies/Shutterbugs', 'News & Politics/Avid News Readers/Entertainment News Enthusiasts', 'Media & Entertainment/Music Lovers', and more...\n    - medium: (none), organic, referral, cpc\n    - page: '/', '/company', '/waitlist', '/product', '/ai-marketing-agent-system', '/careers', '/careers/founding-full-stack-engineer', '/careers/founding-data-engineer', '/blog', '/careers/founding-ai-engineer', and more...\n    - source: (direct), google, linkedin.com, syndicatedsearch.goog, wake-up-network.com\n\n    Each record in the table conforms to the following schema model:\n\n    ```python\n    class WebsiteStats(DataFrameModel):\n        \"\"\"The stats of a website over a given window of time, measured on a specific date.\n\n        These statistics are aggregated for a specific dimension (e.g. country, language, etc.) or for the overall account ('all').\n        \"\"\"\n\n        platform: pl.Enum(categories=[\"web\"]) = Field(  # type: ignore\n            description=(\n                \"The data-source connector these stats are from (always `web` for GA4), or `all` if it's the \"\n                \"overall stats. GA4's device/app platform (web/iOS/Android) is a separate breakdown queried as \"\n                \"`dim_name='ga4_platform'` — the `ga4_` prefix exists to avoid colliding with this column\"\n            )\n        )\n        id: str = Field(\n            description=\"The unique ID of the account on the platform. In case `platform` is `all`, this should be same as `domain`\"\n        )\n        domain: str = Field(description=\"The DOJO AI domain of the account\")\n\n        # Read-path discoverability superset: every dimension queryable live from GA4, not a\n        # producer contract (the dormant ELT pipeline emits a narrower set).\n        dim_name: pl.Enum(\n            categories=[\n                \"page\",\n                \"age\",\n                \"gender\",\n                \"interest\",\n                \"country\",\n                \"source\",\n                \"medium\",\n                \"new_vs_returning\",\n                \"default_channel_group\",\n                \"ga4_platform\",\n                \"operating_system\",\n                \"stream_id\",\n                \"mobile_device_branding\",\n                \"all\",\n            ]\n        ) = Field(  # type: ignore\n            description=\"The name of the dimension or `all` if it's the overall stats\"\n        )\n        dim_value: str = Field(description=\"The value of the dimension or `all` if it's the overall stats\")\n\n        # we standardize all date and datetimes to the same type so that joins and\n        # df manipulations don't yield errors, when the agents are using them\n        day: datetime.datetime = Field(description=\"The day of the stats\")\n        agg_window_in_days: int = Field(\n            description=\"The number of days the stats report to\", ge=0\n        )  # TODO: change this to a TimeDelta\n\n        recorded_at: datetime.datetime = Field(\n            description=\"The timestamp of when this record was calculated and stored in the datalake, in UTC\"\n        )\n        synced_at: datetime.datetime = Field(\n            description=\"The timestamp of the latest synced data used to calculate this record, in UTC\"\n        )\n\n        n_pageviews: int = Field(description=\"The number of page views\", ge=0)\n        n_sessions: int = Field(\n            description=\"The number of sessions initiated by users. A session begins when a user opens the website or app and ends after 30 minutes of inactivity\",\n            ge=0,\n        )\n        n_uniques: int = Field(description=\"The number of unique users who have had at least one session\", ge=0)\n        n_new_users: int = Field(\n            description=\"The number of users (uniques) visiting the website for the first time ever\",\n            ge=0,\n        )\n\n        n_engaged_sessions: int = Field(description=\"The number of sessions where the user was actively engaged\", ge=0)\n        engagement_rate: float = Field(\n            description=\"The number of engaged sessions per number of sessions\",\n            ge=0,\n            nullable=True,\n        )\n        average_session_duration: float = Field(description=\"The average duration of a session\", ge=0, nullable=True)\n        total_engagement_duration: float | None = Field(\n            description=\"The total amount of time (in seconds) your website or app was in the foreground of users` devices.\",\n            ge=0,\n        )\n        total_revenue: float = Field(\n            description=\"The revenue generated by users, including purchases and other monetary transactions on the website. Can be negative due to product returns\",\n        )\n\n        class Config(BaseConfig):\n            unique = [\"platform\", \"id\", \"domain\", \"dim_name\", \"dim_value\", \"day\"]\n\n    ```\n\n    #### Table: website_account_event_daily_stats\n\n    **Description:** Stats of the customer's website events, possibly grouped by dimensions such as page or country, aggregated over the last 2 years (2*365 days).\n    **Temporal Aggregation:** 1 days\n    **Dimensions:**\n    - all: all\n    - age: unknown, 18-24, 25-34, 35-44, 45-54, 55-64, 65+\n    - country: 'United States', 'United Kingdom', 'Germany', 'Canada', 'Australia', 'France', 'Spain', 'Italy', 'Netherlands', 'Sweden', and more...\n    - gender: male, female, unknown\n    - interest: 'Technology/Technophiles', 'News & Politics/Avid News Readers', 'Travel/Travel Buffs', 'Sports & Fitness/Sports Fans', 'Banking & Finance/Avid Investors', 'Media & Entertainment/Music Lovers', 'Lifestyles & Hobbies/Business Professionals', 'Food & Dining/Cooking Enthusiasts', 'Shopping/Shoppers', 'Arts & Entertainment/Movie Lovers', and more...\n    - medium: '(none)', 'organic', 'referral', '(not set)', 'cpc', 'email', '(data not available)', 'social', 'paid_social', 'display', and more...\n    - page: '/', '(not set)', '/about', '/contact', '/products', '/services', '/blog', '/careers', '/login', '/search', and more...\n    - source: '(direct)', 'google', '(not set)', 'bing', 'facebook', 'linkedin.com', 'twitter', 'instagram', 'youtube', 'reddit', and more...\n    - new_vs_returning: new, returning, (not set)\n    - default_channel_group: 'Direct', 'Display', 'Email', 'Organic Search', 'Organic Social', 'Paid Search', 'Referral', 'Cross-network', 'Unassigned', 'and more...', and more...\n    - file_name: /whitepapers/annual_report.pdf, /docs/getting_started.pdf, /assets/brochure.pdf, (not set), and more...\n    - link_url: https://example.com/whitepapers/annual_report.pdf, https://partner.example.org/signup, https://docs.example.com/api, (not set), and more...\n    - ga4_platform: web, iOS, Android\n    - operating_system: Windows, Android, iOS, Macintosh, Linux, Chrome OS, (not set), and more...\n    - stream_id: 1234567890, 0987654321, and more...\n    - mobile_device_branding: Apple, Samsung, Google, Xiaomi, (not set), and more...\n\n    Each record in the table conforms to the following schema model:\n\n    ```python\n    class WebsiteEventStats(DataFrameModel):\n        \"\"\"The event stats of a website over a given window of time, measured on a specific date.\n\n        These statistics are aggregated for a specific event type and dimension (e.g. country, language, etc.) or for the overall account ('all').\n        \"\"\"\n\n        platform: pl.Enum(categories=[\"web\"]) = Field(  # type: ignore\n            description=(\n                \"The data-source connector these stats are from (always `web` for GA4), or `all` if it's the \"\n                \"overall stats. GA4's device/app platform (web/iOS/Android) is a separate breakdown queried as \"\n                \"`dim_name='ga4_platform'` — the `ga4_` prefix exists to avoid colliding with this column\"\n            )\n        )\n        id: str = Field(  # GA4 Property ID\n            description=\"The unique ID of the account on the platform. In case `platform` is `all`, this should be same as `domain`\"\n        )\n        domain: str = Field(description=\"The DOJO AI domain of the account\")\n\n        event_name: str = Field(description=\"The name of the event (e.g., 'add_to_cart', 'checkout')\")\n        is_key_event: bool = Field(\n            description=\"True if this event was marked and counted as a key event (conversion) for this period.\"\n        )\n\n        # Read-path discoverability superset: every dimension queryable live from GA4, not a\n        # producer contract (the dormant ELT pipeline emits a narrower set).\n        dim_name: pl.Enum(\n            categories=[\n                \"page\",\n                \"age\",\n                \"gender\",\n                \"interest\",\n                \"country\",\n                \"source\",\n                \"medium\",\n                \"new_vs_returning\",\n                \"default_channel_group\",\n                \"file_name\",\n                \"link_url\",\n                \"ga4_platform\",\n                \"operating_system\",\n                \"stream_id\",\n                \"mobile_device_branding\",\n                \"all\",\n            ]\n        ) = Field(  # type: ignore\n            description=\"The name of the dimension or `all` if it's the overall stats\"\n        )\n        dim_value: str = Field(description=\"The value of the dimension or `all` if it's the overall stats\")\n\n        day: datetime.date = Field(description=\"The day of the stats (end-of-day)\")\n        agg_window_in_days: int = Field(\n            description=\"The number of days the stats report to\", ge=0\n        )  # TODO: change this to a TimeDelta\n\n        recorded_at: datetime.datetime = Field(\n            description=\"The timestamp of when this record was calculated and stored in the datalake, in UTC\"\n        )\n        synced_at: datetime.datetime = Field(\n            description=\"The timestamp of the latest synced data used to calculate this record, in UTC\"\n        )\n\n        n_events: int = Field(description=\"Total number of times this event occurred\", ge=0)\n        n_uniques: int = Field(\n            description=\"Number of users (uniques) who triggered this event at least once\",\n            ge=0,\n        )\n        events_per_user_rate: float = Field(\n            description=\"Average number of times this event was triggered per unique user (n_events / n_uniques).\",\n            ge=0.0,\n            nullable=True,  # Can be null if n_uniques is 0\n        )\n        total_revenue: float | None = Field(\n            description=\"Total revenue attributed to or associated with this event for the given dimensions and day. Can be negative due to product returns\",\n            nullable=True,\n        )\n\n        class Config(BaseConfig):\n            unique = [\"platform\", \"id\", \"domain\", \"event_name\", \"dim_name\", \"dim_value\", \"day\"]\n\n    ```\n\n    #### Table: website_account_event_last_year_stats\n\n    **Description:** Stats of the customer's website events, possibly grouped by dimensions such as page or country, aggregated over the last 2 years (2*365 days).\n    **Temporal Aggregation:** 365 days\n    **Dimensions:**\n    - all: all\n    - age: unknown, 18-24, 25-34, 35-44, 45-54, 55-64, 65+\n    - country: 'United States', 'United Kingdom', 'Germany', 'Canada', 'Australia', 'France', 'Spain', 'Italy', 'Netherlands', 'Sweden', and more...\n    - gender: male, female, unknown\n    - interest: 'Technology/Technophiles', 'News & Politics/Avid News Readers', 'Travel/Travel Buffs', 'Sports & Fitness/Sports Fans', 'Banking & Finance/Avid Investors', 'Media & Entertainment/Music Lovers', 'Lifestyles & Hobbies/Business Professionals', 'Food & Dining/Cooking Enthusiasts', 'Shopping/Shoppers', 'Arts & Entertainment/Movie Lovers', and more...\n    - medium: '(none)', 'organic', 'referral', 'cpc', '(not set)', 'email', 'social', 'paid_social', 'affiliate', 'display', and more...\n    - page: '/', '(not set)', '/about', '/contact', '/products', '/services', '/blog', '/careers', '/login', '/search', and more...\n    - source: '(direct)', 'google', 'bing', '(not set)', 'facebook', 'linkedin.com', 'twitter', 'instagram', 'youtube', 'reddit', and more...\n    - new_vs_returning: new, returning, (not set)\n    - default_channel_group: 'Direct', 'Display', 'Email', 'Organic Search', 'Organic Social', 'Paid Search', 'Referral', 'Cross-network', 'Unassigned', 'and more...', and more...\n    - file_name: /whitepapers/annual_report.pdf, /docs/getting_started.pdf, /assets/brochure.pdf, (not set), and more...\n    - link_url: https://example.com/whitepapers/annual_report.pdf, https://partner.example.org/signup, https://docs.example.com/api, (not set), and more...\n    - ga4_platform: web, iOS, Android\n    - operating_system: Windows, Android, iOS, Macintosh, Linux, Chrome OS, (not set), and more...\n    - stream_id: 1234567890, 0987654321, and more...\n    - mobile_device_branding: Apple, Samsung, Google, Xiaomi, (not set), and more...\n\n    Each record in the table conforms to the following schema model:\n\n    ```python\n    class WebsiteEventStats(DataFrameModel):\n        \"\"\"The event stats of a website over a given window of time, measured on a specific date.\n\n        These statistics are aggregated for a specific event type and dimension (e.g. country, language, etc.) or for the overall account ('all').\n        \"\"\"\n\n        platform: pl.Enum(categories=[\"web\"]) = Field(  # type: ignore\n            description=(\n                \"The data-source connector these stats are from (always `web` for GA4), or `all` if it's the \"\n                \"overall stats. GA4's device/app platform (web/iOS/Android) is a separate breakdown queried as \"\n                \"`dim_name='ga4_platform'` — the `ga4_` prefix exists to avoid colliding with this column\"\n            )\n        )\n        id: str = Field(  # GA4 Property ID\n            description=\"The unique ID of the account on the platform. In case `platform` is `all`, this should be same as `domain`\"\n        )\n        domain: str = Field(description=\"The DOJO AI domain of the account\")\n\n        event_name: str = Field(description=\"The name of the event (e.g., 'add_to_cart', 'checkout')\")\n        is_key_event: bool = Field(\n            description=\"True if this event was marked and counted as a key event (conversion) for this period.\"\n        )\n\n        # Read-path discoverability superset: every dimension queryable live from GA4, not a\n        # producer contract (the dormant ELT pipeline emits a narrower set).\n        dim_name: pl.Enum(\n            categories=[\n                \"page\",\n                \"age\",\n                \"gender\",\n                \"interest\",\n                \"country\",\n                \"source\",\n                \"medium\",\n                \"new_vs_returning\",\n                \"default_channel_group\",\n                \"file_name\",\n                \"link_url\",\n                \"ga4_platform\",\n                \"operating_system\",\n                \"stream_id\",\n                \"mobile_device_branding\",\n                \"all\",\n            ]\n        ) = Field(  # type: ignore\n            description=\"The name of the dimension or `all` if it's the overall stats\"\n        )\n        dim_value: str = Field(description=\"The value of the dimension or `all` if it's the overall stats\")\n\n        day: datetime.date = Field(description=\"The day of the stats (end-of-day)\")\n        agg_window_in_days: int = Field(\n            description=\"The number of days the stats report to\", ge=0\n        )  # TODO: change this to a TimeDelta\n\n        recorded_at: datetime.datetime = Field(\n            description=\"The timestamp of when this record was calculated and stored in the datalake, in UTC\"\n        )\n        synced_at: datetime.datetime = Field(\n            description=\"The timestamp of the latest synced data used to calculate this record, in UTC\"\n        )\n\n        n_events: int = Field(description=\"Total number of times this event occurred\", ge=0)\n        n_uniques: int = Field(\n            description=\"Number of users (uniques) who triggered this event at least once\",\n            ge=0,\n        )\n        events_per_user_rate: float = Field(\n            description=\"Average number of times this event was triggered per unique user (n_events / n_uniques).\",\n            ge=0.0,\n            nullable=True,  # Can be null if n_uniques is 0\n        )\n        total_revenue: float | None = Field(\n            description=\"Total revenue attributed to or associated with this event for the given dimensions and day. Can be negative due to product returns\",\n            nullable=True,\n        )\n\n        class Config(BaseConfig):\n            unique = [\"platform\", \"id\", \"domain\", \"event_name\", \"dim_name\", \"dim_value\", \"day\"]\n\n    ```\n\n    #### Table: social_posts_content_analysis\n\n    **Description:** The natural language processing analysis of a post on a social media or content platform. It extracts things like sentiment, emotions, topics, keywords, entities, style, summaries, etc..\n    **Temporal Aggregation:** N/A.\n    **Dimensions:** N/A.\n\n    Each record in the table conforms to the following schema model:\n\n    ```python\n    class SocialPostContentAnalysis(DataFrameModel):\n        \"\"\"The natural language processing analysis of a post on a social media or content platform.\n\n        Only includes posts that have significant content to analyze, excluding comments, polls and posts without enough text to analyze.\n        \"\"\"\n\n        platform: pl.Enum(categories=[\"linkedin\", \"twitter\", \"facebook\", \"instagram\"]) = Field(  # type: ignore\n            description=\"The platform of the post\"\n        )\n        account_id: str = Field(description=\"The ID of the account that made this post\")\n        domain: str = Field(description=\"The DOJO AI domain of the account\")\n        post_id: str = Field(description=\"The ID of the post\")\n\n        content: str = Field(description=\"The content that was analyzed\")\n\n        created_at: datetime.datetime = Field(description=\"The creation date of the post\")\n        updated_at: datetime.datetime = Field(description=\"The last update date of the post\")\n        recorded_at: datetime.datetime = Field(description=\"The date when the post analysis was recorded in the datalake\")\n\n        # ContentAnalysis fields\n        emotions: pl.List = Field(\n            description=f\"The main emotions of the post. Can be one of {', '.join(e.value for e in Emotion)}\",\n            dtype_kwargs={\"inner\": pl.Enum(categories=[e.value for e in Emotion])},\n        )\n        sentiment: pl.Enum(categories=[v.value for v in Sentiment]) = Field(description=\"The sentiment of the post\")  # type: ignore\n        oneliner: str = Field(description=\"A one-liner summaryof the post\")\n        summary: str = Field(description=\"A summary of the post\")\n        topics: pl.List = Field(description=\"The main topics of the post\", dtype_kwargs={\"inner\": pl.String})\n        keywords: pl.List = Field(description=\"The main keywords of the post\", dtype_kwargs={\"inner\": pl.String})\n        entities: pl.List = Field(description=\"The main entities of the post\", dtype_kwargs={\"inner\": pl.String})\n        word_counts: pl.List = Field(\n            description=\"The word counts of the post, as a list of structs with keys 'key' (the word) and 'value' (the count)\",\n            dtype_kwargs={\"inner\": pl.Struct({\"key\": pl.String, \"value\": pl.Int64})},\n        )\n\n        style: str = Field(description=\"The style of the post\")\n\n        # NOTE: the dataframe will actually have a struct with the four ToneOfVoice components instead of four top-level columns\n        # -> tone_of_voice: pl.Struct = Field(description=\"The tone of voice of the post, according to the Nielsen Norman Group dimensions in a ternary scale (-1, 0, 1): Formal vs Casual, Serious vs Funny, Respectful vs Irreverent, Matter-of-Fact vs Enthusiastic\", dtype_kwargs={\"fields\": pl.Struct({\"formal_or_casual\": pl.Int8, \"serious_or_funny\": pl.Int8, \"respectful_or_irreverent\": pl.Int8, \"matter_of_fact_or_enthusiastic\": pl.Int8})})\n        tone_of_voice_formal_or_casual: pl.Int8 = Field(\n            description=\"The tone of voice of the post, according to the Nielsen Norman Group dimensions in a ternary scale (-1, 0, 1): Formal vs Casual\",\n            isin=[-1, 0, 1],\n        )\n        tone_of_voice_serious_or_funny: pl.Int8 = Field(\n            description=\"The tone of voice of the post, according to the Nielsen Norman Group dimensions in a ternary scale (-1, 0, 1): Serious vs Funny\",\n            isin=[-1, 0, 1],\n        )\n        tone_of_voice_respectful_or_irreverent: pl.Int8 = Field(\n            description=\"The tone of voice of the post, according to the Nielsen Norman Group dimensions in a ternary scale (-1, 0, 1): Respectful vs Irreverent\",\n            isin=[-1, 0, 1],\n        )\n        tone_of_voice_matter_of_fact_or_enthusiastic: pl.Int8 = Field(\n            description=\"The tone of voice of the post, according to the Nielsen Norman Group dimensions in a ternary scale (-1, 0, 1): Matter-of-Fact vs Enthusiastic\",\n            isin=[-1, 0, 1],\n        )\n\n    ```\n    \"\"\"\n    ...\n\nasync def get_google_ads_analytics(campaign_id: int | None = None, ad_group_id: int | None = None, ad_id: int | None = None, conversion_action_id: int | None = None, time_dimension: Optional[Literal['hour', 'date', 'day_of_week', 'week', 'month', 'month_of_year', 'quarter', 'year']] = None, segment_dimension: Optional[Literal['device', 'ad_format_type', 'ad_network_type', 'external_conversion_source', 'conversion_action', 'conversion_action_name', 'conversion_action_category', 'new_versus_returning_customers', 'slot', 'campaign']] = None, start_date: datetime.date | None = None, end_date: datetime.date | None = None) -> pandas.core.frame.DataFrame | None:\n    \"\"\"Get a dataframe of Google Ads analytics data.\n\n    Retrieve detailed Google Ads performance analytics at the account, campaign, ad group, or ad level.\n    Returns metrics including impressions, clicks, cost, and conversion data.\n    You can group by time ('date', 'week', 'month', 'quarter') or by a non-time segment dimension,\n    but not both at the same time.\n\n    Args:\n        campaign_id: Campaign ID to filter by. None for account-level.\n        ad_group_id: Ad group ID to filter by.\n        ad_id: Ad ID to filter by.\n        conversion_action_id: Conversion action ID to filter by.\n        time_dimension: Time granularity to group by ('date', 'week', 'month', 'quarter', or None).\n        segment_dimension: Non-time dimension to segment by (e.g. 'device', 'conversion_action_name').\n        start_date: Start date for analytics data.\n        end_date: End date for analytics data.\n\n    Returns:\n        A DataFrame with the analytics data, or None if no data is found.\n    \"\"\"\n    ...\n", "has_succeeded": true, "artifacts": []}

