data: {"type": "thinking", "id": "t6", "content": "I notice the LinkedIn lifetime stats are missing post counts, but the posts table has 255 entries, so I'll pull the platform-level post counts from there instead. Now I'm building a follower growth chart over time using the daily stats, filtering for the total followers across all platforms each day."}

event: final
data: {"type": "action", "id": "act7", "icon": "chart", "title": "Creating chart", "results": [], "results_units": "Results", "started_at": "2026-08-01T09:02:41.906277Z", "ended_at": "2026-08-01T09:02:46.333197Z", "input": {"source": "\n# Post counts from posts table (more complete than lifetime table's total_posts)\npost_counts = posts['platform'].value_counts().reset_index()\npost_counts.columns = ['platform','post_count']\nfig2b = px.bar(post_counts.sort_values('post_count', ascending=False), x='platform', y='post_count',\n               title='Number of Posts by Platform (from post-level data)', text='post_count')\nfig2b.update_traces(textposition='outside')\nfig2b.show()\n\n# Follower growth over time\ndaily_f = daily[daily['platform']!='all'][['platform','day','total_followers']].dropna().sort_values('day')\nfig3 = px.line(daily_f, x='day', y='total_followers', color='platform', title='Follower Growth Over Time by Platform')\nfig3.show()\n\ndaily_f.groupby('platform')['day'].agg(['min','max','count'])\n"}}

