data: {"type": "thinking", "id": "t7", "content": "Looking at the follower data across platforms, Facebook shows a flat line at 1 (likely just a page follows count), while LinkedIn demonstrates real growth from 2257 to 4979 followers over about 10 months, which aligns with the lifetime max of 5000. Twitter's daily data is missing entirely with no follower counts recorded, though the lifetime data showed 65 followers—I need to investigate why the daily Twitter data is absent.\n\nThe date range for Twitter spans from August 2024 to August 2026, which seems unusual. Looking at the overall follower distribution, LinkedIn dominates by far at 5000, followed by Twitter at 65, Instagram at 8, and Facebook at 1. Now I want to shift focus to engagement metrics like impressions, engagement counts, and engagement rates across platforms over time, then identify the top-performing posts by engagement and examine engagement trends."}

event: final
data: {"type": "action", "id": "act8", "icon": "notebook", "title": "Coding", "results": [], "results_units": "Results", "started_at": "2026-08-01T09:02:53.337419Z", "ended_at": "2026-08-01T09:02:59.464767Z", "input": {"source": "\n# Check twitter followers issue\ntw = daily[daily['platform']=='twitter'][['day','total_followers','n_followers_delta']]\ndisplay(tw.tail(10))\nprint(tw['total_followers'].isna().sum(), len(tw))\n"}}

