data: {"type": "thinking", "id": "t8", "content": "Facebook's sample size is too small with only 4 posts, so that 0.27 engagement rate average isn't reliable—I should flag that. Now I have enough data for the social media overview, so I'll generate an HTML report with inline charts and then ask about moving forward to Google Analytics. Looking at the social media data across all four accounts—LinkedIn's clearly the star with over 109k impressions and strong engagement, Twitter has modest activity, Instagram is just getting started, and Facebook is essentially dormant. The top-performing content is LinkedIn posts, particularly that team collaboration post that hit 1,682 engagements. I'll present these findings with charts and then ask whether you'd like to move into Google Analytics next or explore something else first."}

