data: {"type": "assistant", "id": "a10", "content": "\n\nLinkedIn: 115 media posts, 89 text, 29 articles, 17 carousels. Twitter: mostly text (67 of 74). Instagram: mostly media (9 of 12).\n\n### Average engagement rate by platform\n\n| Platform | Avg. Engagement Rate | # Posts |\n|---|---|---|\n| Facebook | 27.1%* | 4 |\n| LinkedIn | 8.3% | 255 |\n| Twitter/X | 7.9% | 74 |\n| Instagram | 7.1% | 12 |\n\n*Facebook's figure is **not reliable** — based on only 4 posts.\n\n### Top 10 posts by engagement (all LinkedIn)\n| Date | Excerpt | Impressions | Engagements | Engagement Rate |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 2026-02-18 | \"How do you get your entire team posting on LinkedIn...\" | 2,948 | 1,682 | 57.1% |\n| 2024-11-28 | \"This data tells a story... Only 27% of marketing teams...\" | 2,062 | 901 | 43.7% |\n| 2025-02-17 | \"Breakthrough technology needs breakthrough talent...\" | 3,576 | 447 | 12.5% |\n| 2025-05-05 | \"Two mission-critical additions to the DOJO team...\" | 4,198 | 423 | 10.1% |\n| 2026-03-09 | \"Most brands skip the research phase...\" | 795 | 297 | 37.4% |\n| 2026-02-26 | \"'12% of spend? It's piracy, man.'...\" | 978 | 280 | 28.6% |\n| 2024-11-18 | \"Introducing DOJO: The first Marketing Operating System\" | 2,624 | 233 | 8.9% |\n| 2026-01-26 | \"19 testimonials. 10 industries. One pattern.\" | 955 | 227 | 23.8% |\n| 2024-12-04 | \"The 'Martech for 2025' report just dropped...\" | 2,003 | 213 | 10.6% |\n| 2026-05-11 | \"We were on stage and on the floor at @DMWF...\" | 331 | 178 | 53.8% |\n\n**Bottom line:** LinkedIn is by far the primary and most effective social channel (99% of engagements, largest and fastest-growing audience). Twitter has modest reach with no follower tracking. Instagram is nascent (3 months old). Facebook is effectively dormant.\n\n---"}

