data: {"type": "assistant", "id": "a27", "content": "## REPORT: DOJO AI — Combined Data Overview (Social Media + Google Analytics)\n\nI've built the full HTML report and saved it to your Library: **[DOJO AI Data Overview Report.html](outputs/DOJO AI Data Overview Report.html)** (now open in the preview panel), covering everything shown in this chat.\n\n### Summary of what's in it\n**1. Social Media** (LinkedIn, Twitter/X, Facebook, Instagram)\n- LinkedIn dominates: 5,000 followers, 255 posts, 109,387 impressions, 11,237 engagements — ~99% of all engagement across platforms\n- Twitter/X: 65 followers (no daily tracking available), 74 posts, modest reach\n- Instagram: brand-new (created May 2026), 8 followers, 12 posts\n- Facebook: effectively dormant (1 follower, 4 posts) — excluded from rate comparisons as statistically unreliable\n- Top 10 posts by engagement are all LinkedIn, led by a team-posting tip (57.1% engagement rate)\n\n**2. Google Analytics** (example.com, GA4, tracked since 2024-08-06)\n- 104,806 pageviews / 79,505 sessions / 68,897 unique users / 54,150 new users over the full period\n- No revenue/purchases recorded (site is lead-gen, not e-commerce)\n- Direct (34,286 sessions) and Organic Search (23,732) are the largest channels historically\n- A sharp traffic and engagement surge starts June 2026, driven by new Paid Search/Paid Social pushes and a first-ever appearance of \"AI Assistant\" referral traffic\n- Homepage (`/`) drives 58,559 of 104,806 total pageviews; top markets are US, UK, Portugal\n\n### Note on BigQuery\nThe warehouse query failed with an OAuth token error (`invalid_grant` — needs re-authentication), so per your instruction I skipped it and finalized with Social + GA only. I notice the connection now shows as active again in this session — if you'd like, just ask and I can pull the `ad_spend` / `orders` overview as a follow-up and append it to the report."}
